    <summaries>
      <summary>
        <versionCode>07</versionCode>
        <actionDate>2026-10-09</actionDate>
        <actionDesc>Reported to House</actionDesc>
        <updateDate>2026-11-04T13:25:58Z</updateDate>
        <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>SBIC Reporting Modernization Act of 2026</strong></p><p>This bill requires the Small Business Administration (SBA) to report quarterly on its website specified information about Small Business Investment Companies (SBICs), such as the amount of SBA-guaranteed financing SBICs receive. SBICs are privately owned companies, licensed and regulated by the SBA, which invest in small businesses through debt and equity.</p><p>The quarterly report must include (1) elements of the SBA's annual report, such as the number of licensed SBICs and the amount of government leverage each has received; (2) the number of SBIC applicants approved; and (3) the number of jobs created or sustained as a result of SBIC investments. (In general, an SBIC may receive $2 of SBA-guaranteed financing for every $1 in private capital the SBIC raises, subject to a $150 million limit).</p>]]></text>
      </summary>
    </summaries>
